  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is a Timer?</h2>
    <p><b>Timer = Do Something After Some Time.</b> Two types: <b>Once</b> - Do it one time after a delay. <b>Repeat</b> - Do it again and again after every few seconds.</p>
    <p>Example: A popup appears after 3 seconds. A clock updates every 1 second. A quiz auto-submits after 3 minutes. All of these use timers.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Important:</b> JavaScript time is always in <b>milliseconds</b>. 1000 milliseconds = 1 second. So for 3 seconds, you write 3000. For 1 minute, you write 60000.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Clock + Stopwatch + Delay</h2>
    <p>All 3 timers working live:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <h3 style="margin:0">🕐 Live Clock - Updates Every 1 Second</h3>
      <div class="big-clock" id="liveClock">00:00:00</div>
      <hr style="margin:15px 0;border:1px solid #e2e8f0">
      <h3 style="margin:0">⏱️ Stopwatch - setInterval</h3>
      <div class="big-timer" id="stopwatch">00:00</div>
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="startStopwatch()">Start ▶️</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="stopStopwatch()">Stop ⏸️</button>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="resetStopwatch()">Reset ↺</button>
      <hr style="margin:15px 0;border:1px solid #e2e8f0">
      <h3 style="margin:0">⏳ Delay - setTimeout</h3>
      <p id="delayMsg" style="color:#64748b">Click below. Message will appear after 3 seconds.</p>
      <button class="btn" onclick="startDelay()">Show Message After 3 Sec ⏳</button>
    </div>
    <h2>3. All Timers - Full Table</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Timer</th><th>What It Does</th><th>To Stop It</th><th>Use For</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>setTimeout()</b></td><td>Runs ONCE after delay</td><td>clearTimeout()</td><td>Popup after 3 sec, Hide message after 5 sec</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>setInterval()</b></td><td>Runs AGAIN and AGAIN</td><td>clearInterval()</td><td>Clock, Stopwatch, Countdown, Auto-slide</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>4. setTimeout - Run Once After Delay</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Show alert after 3 seconds (3000 ms)</span><br>
<span class="text">setTimeout(function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">alert("3 seconds are over!");</span><br>
<span class="text">}, 3000);</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// With named function</span><br>
<span class="text">function showWelcome() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("msg").innerText = "Welcome!";</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">setTimeout(showWelcome, 2000); // After 2 seconds, run once</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Save timer ID to cancel it later</span><br>
<span class="text">let myTimer = setTimeout(showWelcome, 5000);</span><br>
<span class="text">clearTimeout(myTimer); // Cancel - Will never run</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. setInterval - Run Again and Again</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Count every 1 second</span><br>
<span class="text">let count = 0;</span><br><br>
<span class="text">let timerId = setInterval(function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">count++;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log("Count: " + count);</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (count === 5) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">clearInterval(timerId); // Stop after 5</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log("Stopped!");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}, 1000); // Every 1000 ms = Every 1 second</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Biggest Beginner Mistake:</b> Forgetting to stop setInterval. If you do not call <code>clearInterval()</code>, it will run forever and slow down your page. Always save the ID and stop it when done.</div>
    <h2>6. Live Clock - Real Code</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function showTime() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let now = new Date(); // Current date and time</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let h = now.getHours();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let m = now.getMinutes();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let s = now.getSeconds();</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("clock").innerText = h + ":" + m + ":" + s;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="text">showTime(); // Show at once, do not wait 1 sec</span><br>
<span class="text">setInterval(showTime, 1000); // Then update every 1 sec</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Countdown Timer - 10 to 0</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let timeLeft = 10;</span><br><br>
<span class="text">let countdown = setInterval(function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(timeLeft);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("timer").innerText = timeLeft;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">timeLeft--;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (timeLeft < 0) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">clearInterval(countdown);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("timer").innerText = "Time Up!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}, 1000);</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Complete Example - Auto Hide Message</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"showMessage()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Show Message</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"msg"</span> <span class="attr">style</span>=<span class="val">"display:none;background:green;color:white;padding:10px"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Saved Successfully!</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showMessage() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let msg = document.getElementById("msg");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">msg.style.display = "block"; // Show</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">setTimeout(function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">msg.style.display = "none"; // Hide after 3 sec</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}, 3000);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Countdown - Start from 10, every 1 sec go down. At 0, show "Time Up!" and stop<br>2. Live Clock - Show current time, update every 1 second with setInterval<br>3. Delayed Welcome - On page load, after 2 seconds show alert "Welcome to my website!"</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Time in milliseconds - 1000 = 1 sec | setTimeout(function, ms) = Run ONCE after delay | clearTimeout(id) = Cancel timeout | setInterval(function, ms) = Run AGAIN and AGAIN | clearInterval(id) = Stop interval | Always save timer ID in variable | Always stop interval when done, else it runs forever | new Date() = Current date/time</div>
